WEBVTT

02:21.730 --> 02:24.910
Um, where is Finn?

02:24.910 --> 02:27.720
Welcome, Mr. Apple.

02:27.720 --> 02:30.240
He's on paid leave today 
for personal reasons.

02:30.240 --> 02:31.920
I didn't ask you.

02:31.920 --> 02:33.040
Er...

02:33.040 --> 02:37.050
I'm afraid you may have gotten
the wrong impression the other day.

02:37.050 --> 02:40.320
What you saw was... 
force majeure, shall I say?

02:40.320 --> 02:44.200
If that's the case, then what exactly
 is your relationship with Finn?

02:44.200 --> 02:53.190
Our relationship? Well, I'm his mentor, 
so I guess I'm like a big brother to him.

02:53.550 --> 02:56.100
Whatever! I don't like you!

03:10.300 --> 03:11.360
Give that back!

03:11.360 --> 03:14.880
Come on. Stop reading the same 
book over and over, and let's—

03:14.880 --> 03:15.900
Give it back!

03:17.290 --> 03:18.840
Now you've done it!

03:19.150 --> 03:21.710
You started it by taking my book!

03:21.710 --> 03:23.060
That's enough!

03:23.060 --> 03:26.070
Andy, Sam... What's going on here?

03:26.070 --> 03:29.980
I wanted to play with Sam, 
so I asked him. But he...

03:35.990 --> 03:37.930
What the heck's his problem?!

03:39.290 --> 03:40.110
Hello, Finn.

03:40.610 --> 03:42.210
There's a new face.

03:42.210 --> 03:43.580
He join us recently?

03:43.580 --> 03:45.990
Yeah, his name is Sam.

03:47.120 --> 03:50.590
Every kid who ends up here has their reasons.

03:51.880 --> 03:53.770
It'll take a little while for him
 to get used to us.

03:54.130 --> 03:57.250
I guess so. Oh...

03:58.320 --> 04:00.930
Lindsey, happy birthday!

04:03.540 --> 04:06.510
I've prepared some excellent meat.

04:06.510 --> 04:09.220
Why is the man at the end 
not joining us today?

04:09.640 --> 04:17.650
Did he catch a cold? Was he injured?
Or... did he screw up again?

04:18.450 --> 04:21.030
Ah, I'm so very worried.

04:21.030 --> 04:23.370
Because, you know...

04:25.170 --> 04:26.900
After all...

04:28.690 --> 04:30.520
We're family, right?

04:31.160 --> 04:35.150
Humanity has flourished 
thanks to familial bonds.

04:35.630 --> 04:41.670
People hunted together, ate together,
 and shared what was left.

04:42.280 --> 04:47.040
Small groups became villages, then towns,

04:47.040 --> 04:51.190
and ultimately what we now know as nations.

04:52.170 --> 04:54.020
Just like us, wouldn't you say?

04:54.650 --> 04:57.310
We're not just some mafia.

04:57.310 --> 05:03.190
We're true family, united through power.

05:05.930 --> 05:11.330
Now is the time to show to the world 
the solidarity of Klondike blood.

05:15.930 --> 05:17.330
To family.

05:18.280 --> 05:19.610
To family!

06:08.830 --> 06:10.150
I'm Finn.

06:10.150 --> 06:15.300
I grew up here, so I'm like family, I guess.

06:15.300 --> 06:16.310
No, you're not.

06:17.310 --> 06:19.810
My mom and dad are gone.

06:24.180 --> 06:29.320
The boy who used to sleep in 
that bed was just like you.

06:30.970 --> 06:36.700
He lost everything, including his memory,
and came to Sun Fields alone.

06:38.400 --> 06:41.490
Lindsey said his family 
died in a traffic accident.

06:42.580 --> 06:46.960
All he had was a card, 
which he clung to dearly.

06:47.700 --> 06:52.340
He thought he was all alone
and that life was tiresome.

06:52.870 --> 06:55.970
This card is important to you.

06:56.650 --> 06:59.850
Don't let it go, no matter what happens.

07:00.740 --> 07:04.020
But Lindsey was always by his side, smiling.

07:05.230 --> 07:09.310
Lindsey would read books, bake cakes,

07:09.810 --> 07:12.310
and sleep beside him on stormy nights.

07:12.310 --> 07:18.070
He'd clean the sheets the boy soiled, 
but he'd sure yell when the boy got hurt

07:18.070 --> 07:20.750
after fighting with the neighborhood kids.

07:22.090 --> 07:24.620
The boy lived at Sun Fields 
for a while like that,

07:25.080 --> 07:26.880
until one day, he realized...

07:28.550 --> 07:31.140
This was his family.

07:32.850 --> 07:37.270
And that beam of light
 brightened his life here.

07:39.740 --> 07:46.010
I'm saying Lindsey's our dad, 
and all the other kids are your siblings.

07:46.010 --> 07:47.400
No, they're not.

07:47.830 --> 07:51.870
No one who tries to steal the book
my parents gave me is my sibling.

07:54.280 --> 07:56.280
Lindsey also told me this...

07:56.980 --> 08:00.980
Listen, no matter how much 
they hit you, don't hit back.

08:01.290 --> 08:05.290
If you do, that makes you
 as weak as they are.

08:08.090 --> 08:08.900
But, you know...

08:11.680 --> 08:14.520
Sam, are you weak?

08:16.430 --> 08:20.310
Then I'll let you in on one more secret.

08:27.170 --> 08:30.140
It's a secret hiding spot for your treasures.

08:30.140 --> 08:31.940
Don't tell anyone.

08:34.020 --> 08:35.500
Do come again.

08:40.830 --> 08:42.200
Ready, and...

08:42.430 --> 08:46.330
Happy birthday, Lindsey!

08:47.190 --> 08:49.000
Thank you, everyone.

08:50.780 --> 08:52.970
And here's a gift from me!

08:53.740 --> 08:54.810
Ta-da!

08:54.810 --> 08:56.440
A new apron!

08:56.440 --> 08:59.430
I bought it with the money I earned.

08:59.950 --> 09:02.390
Lindsey, I'm counting on you.

09:02.390 --> 09:04.230
Next year and the year after,

09:04.230 --> 09:09.110
let's keep celebrating your 
birthday here at Sun Fields!

09:11.740 --> 09:12.610
Thank you.

09:14.770 --> 09:17.110
Oh, the chicken should be ready soon.

09:17.610 --> 09:20.030
Finn, would you help me?

09:20.030 --> 09:21.240
Of course.

09:24.120 --> 09:25.690
Looks good!

09:27.210 --> 09:28.710
Hey, Finn.

09:28.710 --> 09:29.490
Hmm?

09:30.480 --> 09:35.260
As you know, the orphanage
 will be shuttered next spring.

09:35.850 --> 09:41.260
I haven't told the kids yet, but I'm 
looking for new homes for them.

09:41.770 --> 09:46.890
So please don't say anything
 to give them false hope.

09:48.640 --> 09:49.650
Check it out.

09:51.780 --> 09:54.150
How did you get that much money?

09:54.150 --> 09:58.000
I'll be a full-time employee soon,
 and then I can make even more.

09:58.000 --> 10:02.280
Then I'll buy the property, so 
we can keep running Sun Fields.

10:02.820 --> 10:04.230
And if that's not enough,

10:04.230 --> 10:07.410
I can ask Leo, the branch manager, 
for an advance on my pay.

10:08.640 --> 10:09.850
I can't accept this.

10:09.850 --> 10:10.790
What?

10:11.690 --> 10:14.250
You just started working,
 yet you're already making so much?

10:15.050 --> 10:17.450
Have you gotten into something dangerous?

10:17.450 --> 10:19.400
N-No...

10:20.480 --> 10:24.280
Finn, I can't tell you how happy I am

10:24.280 --> 10:26.920
that you'd come visit after graduating.

10:27.530 --> 10:29.190
But in truth...

10:31.050 --> 10:37.340
In truth, I'd be much happier 
if you didn't come back here at all.

10:40.050 --> 10:43.690
Happy birthday to you!

10:43.690 --> 10:46.830
Happy birthday to you!

10:47.380 --> 10:52.960
Happy birthday, dear Lindsey!

10:52.960 --> 10:57.340
Happy birthday to you!

10:52.960 --> 10:57.340
Happy... birthday... to... you...

11:02.900 --> 11:04.100
Thank you all!

11:10.340 --> 11:13.780
Happy birthday to you...

11:13.780 --> 11:17.490
Happy birthday to you...

11:17.490 --> 11:20.660
Happy birthday, dear...

11:22.110 --> 11:23.270
Hey, kid.

11:23.700 --> 11:25.990
What's this dude's name?

11:27.080 --> 11:28.260
You...

11:30.050 --> 11:33.000
Hey, it's been a while.

11:36.960 --> 11:42.430
Why so cold? 
You didn't invite me, Bobby Ball.

11:42.710 --> 11:44.400
Do you know this man, Finn?

11:45.790 --> 11:48.050
I brought a gift.

11:48.050 --> 11:50.740
Oh, that's a nice apron.

11:51.540 --> 11:54.730
Tailored at the storied boutique 
on Old Maid Street...

11:56.090 --> 11:57.070
wasn't it?

11:59.750 --> 12:01.990
Are you a colleague of Finn's?

12:02.590 --> 12:04.340
Thank you for coming.

12:05.230 --> 12:06.630
Lindsey, no!

12:07.660 --> 12:08.430
Play!

12:11.430 --> 12:12.620
What'd you come for?

12:14.010 --> 12:15.920
Isn't it obvious?

12:16.250 --> 12:19.380
To enjoy the party!

12:27.470 --> 12:28.760
Go on now. Run.

12:28.760 --> 12:30.260
Lindsey, get the kids!

12:30.890 --> 12:32.600
Everyone, this way!

12:34.300 --> 12:36.350
This party's a real blast.

12:36.750 --> 12:38.110
Why're you here?

12:38.470 --> 12:41.850
I'm the type to look into people I hate

12:41.850 --> 12:45.870
and chase them to the edge of hell.

12:46.220 --> 12:50.740
I got beat by an amateur like 
you because of beginner's luck,

12:51.040 --> 12:54.050
and Pinochle got the card in the end.

12:54.050 --> 12:57.050
The boss's trust in me has hit rock bottom,

12:57.050 --> 13:01.630
so I get stuck all the way down 
at the end of the table these days.

13:02.070 --> 13:05.290
My shoulder aches where you shot me, y'know?

13:05.290 --> 13:09.890
I gotta repay this debt by going all-in!

13:11.670 --> 13:14.310
Don't get cocky with 
a weak-ass card like that!

13:14.560 --> 13:20.320
No way in hell am I gonna lose 
to the 2 of spades twice!

13:24.070 --> 13:29.560
I'll destroy you <i>and</i> the place
 you love! Everything!

13:43.300 --> 13:45.470
Eat this! Take—

13:53.260 --> 13:55.320
Things are heating up.

13:57.190 --> 13:59.210
Yes! Yes, that's right!

13:59.210 --> 14:00.630
Please come quickly!

14:00.630 --> 14:02.320
Lindsey, Sam is missing!

14:02.320 --> 14:02.940
What?!

14:25.710 --> 14:27.360
What the...?

14:41.940 --> 14:42.630
Tch.

14:53.250 --> 14:54.100
Sam!

14:55.290 --> 14:56.250
Come with me!

14:58.290 --> 14:59.430
Listen, Sam.

14:59.770 --> 15:02.010
Cover your mouth with this.

15:02.510 --> 15:04.920
Don't breathe in smoke, okay?

15:04.920 --> 15:05.830
Okay.

15:05.830 --> 15:06.760
Good.

15:17.260 --> 15:21.270
I found you... two little mousies!

15:28.250 --> 15:29.780
No! Don't move!

15:29.780 --> 15:31.080
Finn, are you okay?!

15:31.080 --> 15:32.800
Yeah, I'm fine!

15:37.810 --> 15:38.780
This way!

15:39.830 --> 15:42.010
Run, run away!

15:50.270 --> 15:52.730
Watch your feet, Sam.

15:54.050 --> 15:55.030
Finn...

15:55.390 --> 15:56.660
It'll be okay.

15:56.990 --> 15:58.310
Let's go up.

16:11.000 --> 16:14.920
<i>Damn it... Why am I...
 at a time like this...</i>

16:19.080 --> 16:23.960
Just how far is the weak little
2 of spades going to run?

16:24.860 --> 16:29.710
The nice man brought 
you something you forgot!

16:30.040 --> 16:31.010
My book!

16:31.010 --> 16:32.090
Give it back!

16:35.960 --> 16:37.220
Sam! Finn!

16:40.410 --> 16:41.350
Over here!

16:44.410 --> 16:45.600
You guys...

16:51.950 --> 16:53.140
Go, Sam!

16:53.140 --> 16:54.110
But...

16:54.530 --> 16:57.130
You can trust my family.

17:07.560 --> 17:13.440
Now, then... I might be weak, 
but I'll do my damnedest.

17:13.440 --> 17:17.010
Good. You're in the mood to play now.

17:17.670 --> 17:20.640
We can't party otherwise.

17:25.820 --> 17:28.650
Here's something Lindsey used 
to tell me when I was small.

17:29.260 --> 17:32.150
Only the weak hit back when they're struck!

17:32.580 --> 17:34.500
Oh, yeah? That so?

17:36.770 --> 17:39.160
I may be weak, but...

17:40.040 --> 17:44.910
But, you know, Finn, getting beaten up
 all the time can be really hard.

17:45.630 --> 17:47.580
Five shots means you're out of ammo!

17:47.970 --> 17:51.670
It's time for you... to explode!

17:53.610 --> 17:56.470
So, if it's someone bad enough...

17:57.290 --> 17:59.430
then beat the living daylights out of them!

18:26.040 --> 18:29.120
Think you can make a fool of me?

18:29.450 --> 18:31.250
Two cards?

18:33.920 --> 18:35.260
Play!

18:35.260 --> 18:37.130
X-Hand!

19:00.430 --> 19:03.520
I feel a surge of power.

19:03.520 --> 19:05.490
Like I've been reborn.

19:05.890 --> 19:10.530
Incredible! Just incredible!
X-Hand is truly amazing!

19:10.530 --> 19:12.380
"X-Hand"?

19:49.050 --> 19:52.540
Why don't we keep the party
 going a little longer?

19:55.310 --> 19:55.920
Finn!

20:10.140 --> 20:13.690
I did my research 
before coming here, you know?

20:16.350 --> 20:21.110
I hear your place went up
 in flames just like this.

20:21.110 --> 20:22.200
Wha...

20:22.200 --> 20:27.830
And you were found in the charred 
ruins of your sorry home!

20:46.330 --> 20:48.660
That's it! Perfect!

20:49.130 --> 20:51.600
Suffer more!

20:51.600 --> 20:57.110
Then let's end everything 
and explode together!

21:12.550 --> 21:15.000
Y-You...

21:15.000 --> 21:19.500
You shitty family!

23:01.990 --> 23:04.270
Finn! Are you all right?!

23:04.980 --> 23:06.110
I'm so glad.

23:06.110 --> 23:09.280
Everyone's okay, and nothing was lost.

23:10.180 --> 23:14.730
No, we lost everything.

23:17.210 --> 23:20.250
Lindsey, have you been lying to me?

23:20.570 --> 23:21.290
Huh?

23:22.090 --> 23:23.350
I remembered.

23:23.980 --> 23:25.770
It wasn't a traffic accident.

23:26.500 --> 23:31.760
My house burned down, just like this,
 and my family was...

23:33.070 --> 23:34.580
By that black knight...

23:36.070 --> 23:38.760
Next time: "BY YOUR SIDE."
